Reason: tests for the AudioToolbox AAC change.
- FFmpeg AAC cases skip when FFmpeg has no AAC decoder (ours doesn't).
- AudioToolbox gets an AAC case from MP4 (bear-mpeg2-aac-only_frag.mp4);
  FFmpeg can't time ADTS streams without its decoder.
- The ADTS AudioSpecificConfig extraction covers AudioToolbox too.
- Without FFmpeg's AAC decoder, FFmpeg reports xHE-AAC mono's container
  channel count instead of "unsupported"; the layout check allows that.
Run October 18 (*AudioToolbox*:FFmpeg/AudioDecoderTest*): 225 tests, all
passed (30 FFmpeg AAC cases skipped). No upstream bug.

diff --git a/media/filters/audio_decoder_unittest.cc b/media/filters/audio_decoder_unittest.cc
index 37897d6d54..6fd7e7c6bb 100644
